<binaryimage arch="ARM:LE:32:v8:default">
<!--
    kuna: a caller that hands back a callee's 64-bit result with only the
    high word changed returns all eight bytes, not void.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 return recovery, the output trials of the
    function's own RETURN (ActionReturnRecovery, p4_calls/kuna_retcallhalf.rs).
    A strict fix: no option.

    Source (clang -target arm-linux-gnueabi -O2, bytes verbatim below; the
    last three functions are hand-written controls):

        typedef unsigned long long u64;
        typedef long long s64;
        u64 full(unsigned a) { return ((u64)(a + 1) << 32) | (a * 3u); }
        int g32s(int a) { return a * 7 - 100; }
        u64 full_or(unsigned a) { return full(a) | 0xff00000000ULL; }
        u64 full_add(unsigned a) { return full(a) + (1ULL << 32); }
        u64 hi_const(unsigned a) { return (7ULL << 32) | (unsigned)g32s(a); }
        s64 sext(int a) { return g32s(a); }
        u64 lo_or(unsigned a) { return full(a) | 0xff; }

        vdiv:  push {r4,lr}; mov r4,r1; bl g32s; ldr r2,=0x51eb851f;
               smull r1,r3,r2,r4; asr r3,r3,#5; sub r3,r3,r4,asr #31;
               ldr r2,=0x2000; str r3,[r2]; pop {r4,pc}
        keepz: push {r11,lr}; bl g32s; mov r1,#0; mov r2,#0; mov r3,#0;
               pop {r11,pc}
        popd:  push {r0,r1,r4,lr}; mov r0,sp; bl g32s; pop {r1,r2,r4,pc}
        sysafter: push {r7,lr}; bl g32s; mov r1,#5; mov r7,#4; svc #0;
               pop {r7,lr}; bx lr

    full_or is bl full ; orr r1,r1,#255 ; pop {r11,lr} ; bx lr.

    The bug: r0 reaches the RETURN as the call's untouched result, an
    INDIRECT creation that return recovery refuses, and the output model
    never returns r1 without r0, so the four callers printed as void.

    The fix: when the second register of a pair is computed and handed only
    to the RETURN, and the first is a call's untouched result, the function
    returns the pair.  vdiv (the dead low word of an smull), keepz (the zero
    -fzero-call-used-regs leaves in r1), popd (gcc's pop of a dummy register
    into r1) and sysafter (r1 set up for an svc whose p-code does not read
    it) write r1 too and stay void; lo_or, which changes only the low word,
    is byte for byte a 32-bit function as well and keeps its int.
-->
